{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010730-the-effects-of-other-supernaturals-on-kindred-politics","id":1010730,"title":"The effects of other supernaturals on Kindred politics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-01T11:47:01-08:00","id":1010730,"title":"The effects of other supernaturals on Kindred politics","content":"This idea came about while I was working on a side project where I subtly introduce new players to Mage the Awakening 2nd Edition through a Requiem 2nd Edition Chronicle. From that idea a vision of a Lancea et Sanctum dominated city came to mind where the Judges brutally monitor and control Kindred Disciplines and Blood Sorcery, where paranoia runs rampant as the Kindred fear their herd or servitors might be the secret pawns of soul stealing Witch cults that infest the city. Where the Circle of the Crone and the Ordo Dracul patiently wait in the shadows, biding their time before claiming the city and it's secrets for their own. <br /> <br /> And that got me thinking...<br /> <br /> How would some of the other supernatural creatures effect the development of Kindred politics within a city? What form would Kindred Society take when a sizable portion of the city's populace are other monster? What ideas come to mind when there's more pressing matters than your fellow bloodthirsty Kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 12-01-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:43:10-08:00","id":1010829,"title":"","content":"In my current Mage Chronicle the city has an exceptionally high vampire population, which is only barely kept in check by the Prince. While the Prince does not have an in-depth understanding of Mage politics, he understands there are different opposing factions. Currently, he is working with the Pentacle (more specifically the Silver Ladder, really) while using the threat of instead supporting the local Seers (and giving them access to mystic sites currently claimed by the Ordo Dracul) as leverage to keep the peace and things favourable for the Kindred. He is quite happy about the current situation. Of course, it is not very idyllic. His spies are quite busy, as are a puissant Theban Sorcerer and an Architect of the Monolith that the Prince made deals with to keep himself protected from Awakened shenanigans as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Other supernaturals exist also in town, but they are of little concern for the Kindred. At least not to the level that the Prince himself has to take charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T16:37:40-08:00","id":1010865,"title":"","content":"In my vampire games there's usually a Liaison, sort of appointed by the Prince but also by werewolves. They act as a sort of mediator between issues. It's potentially a glamorous role, if they're on good terms with many werewolf packs and vampires, as they can be the center of a lot of politics. But it's also a dangerous one, for instance if they aren't on good terms with many packs and some werewolves start tearing vampires to pieces or vampires start preying on some extended pack members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}